<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=wheel">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Transport and navigation</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wheel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">before 4000 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A wheel is a rotating component, usually circular, that turns on an axle; the oldest indirect evidence of wheeled movement, miniature clay wheels found north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>, dates from before 4000 BCE. Pictographs of wheeled wagons at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruk">Uruk</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> date to c. 3500–3350 BCE, and the wooden <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ljubljana">Ljubljana</a> Marshes Wheel from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenia">Slovenia</a> to 3340–3030 BCE. The spoked wheel, first known from the Sintashta culture c. 2000 BCE, allowed lighter and swifter vehicles such as war <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariots</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wheel.jpg" alt="Wheel" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vikiçizer · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tekerlek.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>before 4000 BCE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>North of the Black Sea</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Also arose independently</span>Mesoamerica (wheeled toys) (c. 1500 BCE)</p><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Wheeled vehicles appear almost together in Mesopotamia, the Caucasus and Europe in the 4th millennium BCE; whether they spread from the Near East is debated.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/potters-wheel">Potter's wheel<span>c. 4500 BCE</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">Chariot<span>c. 1950 BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/water-wheel">Water wheel<span>4th century BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/steam-locomotive">Steam locomotive<span>1804</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/bicycle">Bicycle<span>1817</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=wheel">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
